      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Beta-blockers have been shown to have a beneficial effect especially regarding secondary prevention in coronary patients. The reduction in global mortality is most noticeable with respect to sudden death, which suggests an antiarrhythmic effect, but other non-lethal ischaemic events are also less frequent. The explanation of this observation is certainly multifactorial: some results point to a potential action on the development of atherosclerotic lesions. This justifies experimental and clinical studies of this hypothesis with this pharmacological group of drugs."},
